\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  \textsc  {BigAE}{} architecture. Encoder (top) compresses the input to a per-survey latent bottleneck; decoder (bottom) reconstructs the input. All layers use ReLU activations; batch normalization (BN) and dropout are applied in the first two encoder layers only. The anomaly score $S$ is the total per-element mean-squared reconstruction error (Eq.~\ref {eq:score}).}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{4}{\BigAE {} architecture. Encoder (top) compresses the input to a per-survey latent bottleneck; decoder (bottom) reconstructs the input. All layers use ReLU activations; batch normalization (BN) and dropout are applied in the first two encoder layers only. The anomaly score $S$ is the total per-element mean-squared reconstruction error (Eq.~\ref {eq:score})}{figure.1}{}}
