\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Representative spectra illustrating the six main anomaly categories identified across the multi-survey campaign. Black line: observed spectrum; red dashed: \textsc  {BigAE}{} reconstruction. Shaded background regions indicate the DESI B (blue), R (gray), and Z (tan) spectral arms. Anomaly scores are the total per-element MSE (Eq.~\ref {eq:score}). \textbf  {(a)} Baseline normal ELG at $z=0.92$: reconstruction tracks the observed spectrum closely (score $= 2.1$). \textbf  {(b)} Z-dominant high-$z$ QSO candidate at $z=4.52$: complete Gunn--Peterson absorption blueward of Ly$\alpha $ at 6711~\r A\ drives extreme reconstruction residuals (score $= 24.6$). \textbf  {(c)} B-dominant blue-excess anomaly: steep UV rise unlearned by \textsc  {BigAE}{} trained on normal continua (score $= 17.1$). \textbf  {(d)} Multi-band unusual AGN at $z=0.31$: extreme [O\,\textsc  {iii}]/H$\beta $ ratio and anomalous [N\,\textsc  {ii}] strength produce residuals across all three arms (score $= 18.3$). \textbf  {(e)} Uncataloged BAL QSO candidate at $z=0.86$: broad Mg\,\textsc  {ii} absorption trough absent from SIMBAD and Milliquas (score $= 15.8$). \textbf  {(f)} T2 brown dwarf from SDSS DR18 via transfer learning: the DESI-trained model has never encountered deeply red, molecularly blanketed T-dwarf spectra, yielding a catastrophic score of $5.3 \times 10^{10}$.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:example_spectra}{{2}{6}{Representative spectra illustrating the six main anomaly categories identified across the multi-survey campaign. Black line: observed spectrum; red dashed: \BigAE {} reconstruction. Shaded background regions indicate the DESI B (blue), R (gray), and Z (tan) spectral arms. Anomaly scores are the total per-element MSE (Eq.~\ref {eq:score}). \textbf {(a)} Baseline normal ELG at $z=0.92$: reconstruction tracks the observed spectrum closely (score $= 2.1$). \textbf {(b)} Z-dominant high-$z$ QSO candidate at $z=4.52$: complete Gunn--Peterson absorption blueward of Ly$\alpha $ at 6711~\AA \ drives extreme reconstruction residuals (score $= 24.6$). \textbf {(c)} B-dominant blue-excess anomaly: steep UV rise unlearned by \BigAE {} trained on normal continua (score $= 17.1$). \textbf {(d)} Multi-band unusual AGN at $z=0.31$: extreme [O\,\textsc {iii}]/H$\beta $ ratio and anomalous [N\,\textsc {ii}] strength produce residuals across all three arms (score $= 18.3$). \textbf {(e)} Uncataloged BAL QSO candidate at $z=0.86$: broad Mg\,\textsc {ii} absorption trough absent from SIMBAD and Milliquas (score $= 15.8$). \textbf {(f)} T2 brown dwarf from SDSS DR18 via transfer learning: the DESI-trained model has never encountered deeply red, molecularly blanketed T-dwarf spectra, yielding a catastrophic score of $5.3 \times 10^{10}$}{figure.2}{}}
